# Default: normalize every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working
# tree, on every platform. Without this, a Windows checkout inherits Git for
# Windows' core.autocrlf=true and silently gets CRLF working copies of files
# nothing pins below (*.tcl, *.md, *.theme, *.test). That matters here because rio
# PRESERVES a file's line endings on save (AGENTS.md D22) — so a source file that
# flips to CRLF once stays CRLF, and extension payloads and test fixtures would
# carry endings the Linux hosts never see. Pinning it makes the checkout identical
# everywhere regardless of the contributor's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts must check out with CRLF line endings: Windows PowerShell 5.1
# mis-parses some constructs (notably here-strings) in LF-only files. Force native
# Windows endings so a Windows checkout always gets a script PowerShell can parse.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# The POSIX shell scripts stay LF everywhere.
*.sh  text eol=lf
